=> NOTE: weak on absolute value, usable on ORDER. That is the case
   that matters -- choke point ranking depends on ordering edges,
   not on getting each p(e) exactly right. Say this explicitly in
   the report; it is a different conclusion from 'the fit failed'.
=> LOW R2, as PLAN.md sec.4 anticipated. This is a finding, not a failure:
   CVSS cannot recover EPSS because EPSS is trained on exploitation
   telemetry that CVSS deliberately excludes. Objective 2 becomes
   'mapping + measured uncertainty', and objective 4 inherits a
   perturbation size that was measured rather than guessed:
   median relative error 55%, p90 200%.
